{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1316939-other-media-inspirations-for-scion","id":1316939,"title":"Other Media Inspirations for Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-06T21:57:57-07:00","id":1316939,"title":"Other Media Inspirations for Scion","content":"What are some of your thoughts for shows, movies, comics, etc. that feel like a good fit for conversion to Scion or could easily be a Scion story already?<br /> <br /> I am reading Origins and Hilda comes to mind. Hilda could easily be the scion of a currently unnamed Aesir or Vanir father. She explores a world much like our own but where the supernatural is present and regarded as real. Trolls, thunder bird mistaken as the herald of Odin, wood spirits, and giants lurk in the edges. Her two friends could be fated boon companions while the Witch in the library and Alfur, the elven observer, are her guides.<br /> <br /> It fits better than it probably should and I like the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T02:52:18-07:00","id":1316957,"title":"","content":"Saint Seya, the chosen heroes of Athena and their Birthright Armors (Cu = legend 1-2, Ag = legend 3-4 and Au = legend 5-6)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T06:52:46-07:00","id":1316981,"title":"","content":"For comedic games, The Almighty Johnsons TV show would work. For creepy games, adapting some of the concepts from The Magnus Archive podcast would work well, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T19:26:05-07:00","id":1317104,"title":"","content":"The Iron Druid Chronicles <br /> Eric Donner gives me early Supernatural vibes, so I figure that could work too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T05:33:11-07:00","id":1317163,"title":"","content":"I have spent the entirety of the Cloak &amp; Dagger show (which I'm aware is a fairly large departure from the comics) thinking 'this is Scion in a nutshell'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T11:45:17-07:00","id":1317217,"title":"","content":"Echoing Hilda for the tone of Scion. Not everyone runs into elves, spirits, or trolls, but <i>nobody doubts</i> <i>they exist</i>. Trolsberg built a large wall around the city to keep out trolls, and there's penalties for bringing trolls into the city. Giants are a known thing, nobody bats an eyelash at ghosts existing... The only real sign I can recall of things being kept on the down low was when Hilda found that book to summon the Tide Mice, and the Librarian asked to know how she found that section of the library.<br /> <br /> And even that seemed to be less &quot;We can't let the normals know that magic exists&quot; and more &quot;The books in here are dangerous so they're not for circulation&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T12:40:23-07:00","id":1317224,"title":"","content":"I assume no need to go into things already referenced in Origin and Hero like American Gods, Wicked &amp; Divine, and Rick Riordan stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-09T03:51:41-07:00","id":1317323,"title":"","content":"Is it me, or Gods from Pantheons can be run more or less like <i>System Lords</i> from <b>Stargate-SG1</b>? <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://stargate.fandom.com/wiki/System_Lord\" target=\"_blank\">https://stargate.fandom.com/wiki/System_Lord</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-09T03:54:10-07:00","id":1317324,"title":"","content":"<b>Assassin's Creed Odyssey</b> DLC <i><b>Fate of Atlantis</b></i> seems as fun inspiration for Theoi Scions.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bc3vmGo9Sjg&amp;fbclid=IwAR34tQq7vsu-vWEvbi0iUZmdiw8hL_LAeB2N4hsmAaI1PHVOZSjfGDbhMCA\" target=\"_blank\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bc3vmGo9Sjg\" data-code=\"Bc3vmGo9Sjg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Bc3vmGo9Sjg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-09T05:16:41-07:00","id":1317330,"title":"","content":"Hardly an example of the right time period, but <i>Hercules: the Legendary Journeys</i> takes plaice in a world where all cultures\u2019 myths are true, and petty gods use whatever demigod is on hand to further their own ends (when they\u2019re not trying to kill them!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-09T09:52:54-07:00","id":1317367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1316939-other-media-inspirations-for-scion?p=1317330#post1317330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hardly an example of the right time period, but <i>Hercules: the Legendary Journeys</i> takes plaice in a world where all cultures\u2019 myths are true, and petty gods use whatever demigod is on hand to further their own ends (when they\u2019re not trying to kill them!).</div> </div> </div> </div>It dipped into future stuff from time to time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-09T14:32:02-07:00","id":1317406,"title":"","content":"No surprise since it is tangentially related to Sandman, but Lucifer (TV) is an excellent take on an Incarnated Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-09T17:25:47-07:00","id":1317451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1316939-other-media-inspirations-for-scion?p=1317406#post1317406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No surprise since it is tangentially related to Sandman, but Lucifer (TV) is an excellent take on an Incarnated Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think Lucifer is a incarnated Scion. He is more likely an Avatar (I think he is the Angel physically made, not an avatar as he left his position in Hell to be in Earth) than an incarnation. Most of the incarnations have little to no knowledge or memories of their old incarnations at least in the beguinning. Lucifer and all the others are full aware of their lives from the time they step earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-20T02:26:56-07:00","id":1319666,"title":"","content":"<i>Supernatural</i> TV series, <i>American Gods</i> and <i>Tomb Raider</i> franchise ( classical, not 2013 reboot ) are my my main inspirations for Origin Tier in Scion. On <i>Tomb Raider</i> we have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278000-is-scion-origin-like-original-tomb-raider\">whole separate topic</a>. On <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1087902-american-gods\"><i>American Gods</i> inspirations</a> also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And on <i>American Gods</i> as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1302675-2e-new-gods-like-from-american-gods-of-gaiman\">template for running Scion game</a> separated ( with New Gods and all the weird of book world ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T10:03:53-07:00","id":1319961,"title":"","content":"I honestly want to try adapting the Avengers (more so the comics than the films). Also the Justice League, though Grant Morison specifically tried to parallel the team with the Olympians during his run on JLA back in the day.<br /> <br /> I'm also wondering if I can do it with He-Man, Streetfighter, GIJoe, MLP, Sailor Moon, and Jem.<br /> <br /> Because I am weird, even by nerd standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T10:56:58-07:00","id":1319968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1316939-other-media-inspirations-for-scion?p=1319961#post1319961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MLP</div> </div> </div> </div>Psh, I've been doing an on-again off-again project for writing up the Royal Alicorns as possible Patrons.<br /> <br /> Just need their Motif, PSP, and Pantheon Path. &gt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T13:15:02-07:00","id":1320000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1316939-other-media-inspirations-for-scion?p=1319968#post1319968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Psh, I've been doing an on-again off-again project for writing up the Royal Alicorns as possible Patrons.<br /> <br /> Just need their Motif, PSP, and Pantheon Path. &gt;3</div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, I meant using them as inspiration for standard Scion characters spawned by real world gods. But I'd love to see Alicorn Patrons. (Luna is one of my three favorite characters, for a number of reasons.)</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T15:08:52-07:00","id":1320013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1316939-other-media-inspirations-for-scion?p=1319961#post1319961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly want to try adapting the Avengers (more so the comics than the films). Also the Justice League, though Grant Morison specifically tried to parallel the team with the Olympians during his run on JLA back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Grant Morrison, his run of Flex Mentallo might be good to examine. Just replace &quot;superheroes&quot; with &quot;gods.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-21-2019, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T15:25:56-07:00","id":1320016,"title":"","content":"I played once Part Time Gods, and the concept of the game is really nice, more Superheroic than godlike, maybe because of the way we played, but still...<br /> <br /> I would like to try to have a story where all characters are Incarnations of the long lost gods, that for some reason start to popping on earth randomly around the world and learning what they are. There are a few other godlings rising, but none of them are on God level, maybe Demigods still. And the monsters are popping up around too, but not as incarnations, maybe by the act of the Titans or something.<br /> <br /> The final idea is to discover how the gods died and why they are reborn, maybe to avoid the same fate or to repeat so the world live for one more circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T14:05:54-07:00","id":1320147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1316939-other-media-inspirations-for-scion?p=1320013#post1320013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Grant Morrison, his run of Flex Mentallo might be good to examine. Just replace &quot;superheroes&quot; with &quot;gods.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>His entire Doom Patrol run was great. I'm hoping it's possible to do something like Danny the Street in Scion. (Also Fiddlers' Green from Sandman.)<br /> <br /> Flex Mentallo would, I think, make an interesting starting place for the idea of Charles Atlas as a modern god, perhaps part of a pantheon of similar figures. And then something like Luther Strode as one of his Scions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T19:42:21-07:00","id":1321815,"title":"","content":"Check out the graphic novel series 'Wayward' by Jim Zub. A must.<br /> <br /> Everybody mentions 'Sandman' by Gaiman (rightfully so), but as good are the series 'The Books of Magic' by John Ney Rieber and 'Lucifer' by Mike Carey. Both are spin-offs but each rise to their own.<br /> <br /> BTW, The 'Lucifer' TV show has NOTHING to do with the comic. Sadly...<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> <br /> Ken","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3370-ken-winland","name":"Ken Winland","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T18:24:28-08:00","id":1365639,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot;I would like to try to have a story where all characters are Incarnations of the long lost gods, that for some reason start to popping on earth randomly around the world and learning what they are. There are a few other godlings rising, but none of them are on God level, maybe Demigods still. And the monsters are popping up around too, but not as incarnations, maybe by the act of the Titans or something.&quot;<br /> <br /> The gods in their generations perhaps? A new generation of deities every 30,000 years, New gods arrising and dead gods being reborn. Rick Riordan, comic book superheroes, and the Iron Druid Chronicles have all been mentioned. How about The Earth Chronicles by Zecharia Sitchin? Just say he was wrong about the Annunaki being ancient aliens. </span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T02:54:12-08:00","id":1366721,"title":"","content":"I think surprising no one mentioned Ragnar\u00f6k (Netflix) series. I has just one season, six episodes of nearly 40 minutes each. The series has its ups and downs, but I think it gets a lot of &quot;This is Scion: Origin&quot; vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T07:02:19-08:00","id":1366763,"title":"","content":"The new series on Netflix Ragnarok is a great show of Scion as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T21:55:14-08:00","id":1368681,"title":"","content":"It does a lot with a very low budget. I liked it, but it does have a bit of a preachy after-school special vibe to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T13:02:48-08:00","id":1368790,"title":"","content":"Campfire Graphic Novels has a series of books about various Hindu gods/myths, including Krishna, Sita, Hanuman, Ravana, Draupadi, and apparently the Mahabharata as a three part space opera, as well as a couple of Greek ones (Zeus and Perseus, I think). I've read the Krishna one and it's pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/mem